[
  {
    "_comment": "CDC scenario PAUSE AND RESUME: PostgreSQL CDC over logical decoding (wal2json) of the domain's own replication slot (created with the domain, named after it, reused by the publisher); every model table REPLICA IDENTITY FULL, so the two keyless tables log their updates and deletes with whole before-images. wal2json carries the rows an ON DELETE CASCADE takes and an UPDATE that sets the values a row has: --cascades logged --noops logged. The publisher is disabled, the database changes, the publisher is enabled -- 3 times. Enabled again it must resume where it stopped: no change lost, none delivered twice, the initial load not taken again. STAGES: (1) domains -- create the postgrescdc domain, install employeescdc, load the xs seed; (2) actions -- `sentinel-data --key after-create-data`; (3) collections and (4) functions -- register postgrescdc_initial_load (initial_load=True); (5) sentinel -- the load has flushed; then 3 times: actions -- `tdd tdk fn disable`, a 20s pause for the worker to stop, `modify-data --ops Mix --sets 6` and `sentinel-data --key paused-<n>` while it is down, `tdd tdk fn enable`; a sentinel stage holding until paused-<n> arrives; then actions -- one more pass with the publisher running and `sentinel-data --key after-changes`; a sentinel; actions, tagged check -- scripts/verify_cdc_ops.py --start initial-load: one load, and every change after it once, in its transaction, in commit order -- a resume that replayed or skipped is a transaction too many or too few; nothing of audit; monitor. The tdk steps and the check take ${td:profile}: the run's --profile, or tdk's default. Generated by gen_suites.py. Run: `tdd xp one-shot --suite cdc/postgrescdc_pause_resume --keep`."
  },
